<title>USA: Fed refrained from open market intervention.</title>
<headline>Fed refrained from open market intervention.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected the Fed to take no action.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-1/2 percent, the Fed's target for the rate, at the Fed's usual time for open market operations.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
